Z||000000||bryan781||11-11-2001||07:52 PM||||does anyone know of a good preformance injector for the stock fuel system? I have looked around but can only find stock ones.<BR>Thanks <BR>Bryan||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||11-11-2001||08:04 PM||||Jegs or Summit and order Ford Motorsports injectors- available in 19-30 pound per hour. I have a set of 24's in my car and installed a set of 19's in a friends car today. His is a little rich for the stock 2.8, but it is way better than it was before because 4 out of the 6 old ones were leaking pretty bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-11-2001||08:05 PM||||The Fiero store has Tomco injectors but I hear it is better to have your injectors balanced or matched. I think there is a guy here in Connecticut that does this but I don't know who he is or where he is. Maybe someone in the forum knows about this.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||olliver||11-11-2001||08:24 PM||||I think i can be of some assistance on this subject.<P>First of all, unless you have EXTREMELY modified your engine there is absolutely no need to get larger injectors.  I know this for a fact from months and months of pain staking research.<P>The best thing to do is send them to a company the has the means to rebuild them and bench flow them.<P>I just had this done in edmonton.  Very proffesional service.  I'm in cold lake and i just shipped my injectors down to edmonton and he rebuilt them and shipped them back the same day.<P>The company is:<BR>Duke's Injector Service<BR>(780) 960-3388<P>Trust me there is no need for larger injectors unless you have EXTREMELY modified your engine.  Remember the golden rule "more fuel = more air" and if you aren't supplying a large increase in air delivery over stock than there's no need to upgrade your injectors.<P>Olliver<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||11-11-2001||10:06 PM||||What Oliver said only I say there is no need for larger injectors unless you have a nitrous, turbocharger, or a supercharger or you have a super high revving engine.<P>I am running 2.8-injectors on my 3.4 with no problems. It doesn’t go lean either! <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||11-12-2001||09:34 AM||||accel mustang replacements $198 set of 6. 19#/hr will help support on a wet kit at least 280hp. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||grinthock||11-12-2001||11:18 AM||||Called Dukes today, he charges $25 canadain, replaces pintle, screen and flow tests.  Says that 98% of the time he can bring them back to factory specs that way.<P>He said he knows some people in the toronto area and is going to find me someone, REAL nice guy, I gotta reccomend him for at least his customer service||||reg||1
